  title: Kanishka
  text: Kanishka, the greatest Kushana ruler, is usually dated to the late 1st or early 2nd century CE. He patronised Buddhism and convened the Fourth Buddhist Council in Kashmir, and the poet Ashvaghosha and the physician Charaka are associated with his court.
